1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,924
Sweetheart, I've cooked sixty-one Thanksgiving turkeys.

2
00:00:04,104 --> 00:00:05,210
The first one,

3
00:00:05,210 --> 00:00:07,107
in nineteen sixty-three,

4
00:00:07,107 --> 00:00:10,031
was so dry my father-in-law asked for

5
00:00:10,031 --> 00:00:12,718
a glass of water after every bite.

6
00:00:12,898 --> 00:00:14,374
He was a polite man,

7
00:00:14,374 --> 00:00:16,810
so he drank four glasses and said

8
00:00:16,810 --> 00:00:18,065
it was delicious.

9
00:00:18,245 --> 00:00:20,067
I cried in the pantry.

10
00:00:20,247 --> 00:00:22,670
And I swore I'd never serve a

11
00:00:22,670 --> 00:00:24,090
dry turkey again.

12
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:27,674
So tonight I'm giving you my Thanksgiving

13
00:00:27,674 --> 00:00:29,646
turkey, juicy and golden,

14
00:00:29,646 --> 00:00:32,643
every step, and the five mistakes that

15
00:00:32,643 --> 00:00:33,589
make it dry.

16
00:00:33,769 --> 00:00:35,007
And stay with me,

17
00:00:35,007 --> 00:00:38,066
because the last mistake happens after the

18
00:00:38,066 --> 00:00:40,178
turkey comes out of the oven,

19
00:00:40,178 --> 00:00:43,092
and almost every family in America makes

20
00:00:43,092 --> 00:00:44,694
it, every single year.

21
00:00:45,044 --> 00:00:46,492
When I was a girl,

22
00:00:46,492 --> 00:00:49,627
Grandma Pearl raised her own turkeys on

23
00:00:49,627 --> 00:00:50,350
the farm.

24
00:00:50,530 --> 00:00:52,520
She'd pick out the best one in

25
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:54,509
October and feed it corn for a

26
00:00:54,509 --> 00:00:54,907
month.

27
00:00:55,087 --> 00:00:57,834
My brother Danny named it every year,

28
00:00:57,834 --> 00:00:59,987
which was a terrible mistake,

29
00:00:59,987 --> 00:01:02,957
and every Thanksgiving he refused to eat

30
00:01:02,957 --> 00:01:03,179
it.

31
00:01:03,359 --> 00:01:05,774
One year he named it Mr.

32
00:01:05,954 --> 00:01:06,929
Roosevelt.

33
00:01:07,109 --> 00:01:09,458
My father said that was the most

34
00:01:09,458 --> 00:01:11,661
Republican dinner he ever ate.

35
00:01:12,010 --> 00:01:15,024
Back then, people roasted the turkey all

36
00:01:15,024 --> 00:01:16,757
morning, at a low oven,

37
00:01:16,757 --> 00:01:19,319
until it was falling apart and dry

38
00:01:19,319 --> 00:01:20,072
as a bone,

39
00:01:20,072 --> 00:01:22,408
and covered it in gravy to hide

40
00:01:22,408 --> 00:01:22,634
it.

41
00:01:22,814 --> 00:01:25,272
Then in the fifties and sixties the

42
00:01:25,272 --> 00:01:28,363
women's magazines started telling us to cook

43
00:01:28,363 --> 00:01:29,838
it hotter and faster.

44
00:01:30,018 --> 00:01:31,864
My mother didn't trust them.

45
00:01:32,044 --> 00:01:34,162
In a minute I'll tell you which

46
00:01:34,162 --> 00:01:35,666
one of them was right.

47
00:01:36,015 --> 00:01:38,070
First, how big a turkey.

48
00:01:38,250 --> 00:01:40,458
Plan about a pound and a half

49
00:01:40,458 --> 00:01:43,045
per person, so you have leftovers.

50
00:01:43,225 --> 00:01:46,209
A twelve to fourteen pound bird feeds

51
00:01:46,209 --> 00:01:49,112
eight, with sandwiches the next day.

52
00:01:49,292 --> 00:01:51,624
And here's mistake number one,

53
00:01:51,624 --> 00:01:54,655
and it starts days before Thanksgiving.

54
00:01:54,835 --> 00:01:56,821
Not thawing it all the way.

55
00:01:57,001 --> 00:01:59,467
A frozen turkey takes one day in

56
00:01:59,467 --> 00:02:02,011
the icebox for every four or five

57
00:02:02,011 --> 00:02:02,550
pounds.

58
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:05,704
So a fourteen pound turkey needs three

59
00:02:05,704 --> 00:02:07,475
full days in the icebox.

60
00:02:07,655 --> 00:02:10,139
Put it in on Sunday for Thursday.

61
00:02:10,319 --> 00:02:12,575
If the middle is still frozen,

62
00:02:12,575 --> 00:02:15,658
the outside overcooks and dries out while

63
00:02:15,658 --> 00:02:17,838
you wait for the inside to be

64
00:02:17,838 --> 00:02:18,214
done.

65
00:02:18,394 --> 00:02:20,713
And never thaw it on the counter,

66
00:02:20,713 --> 00:02:21,134
honey.

67
00:02:21,314 --> 00:02:23,439
That's how families get sick.

68
00:02:23,619 --> 00:02:24,668
If you're late,

69
00:02:24,668 --> 00:02:26,346
put it in a sink of cold

70
00:02:26,346 --> 00:02:29,004
water, and change the water every half

71
00:02:29,004 --> 00:02:29,354
hour.

72
00:02:29,703 --> 00:02:31,575
Now my best secret,

73
00:02:31,575 --> 00:02:32,954
and it's free.

74
00:02:33,134 --> 00:02:35,400
Salt the turkey a day or two

75
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:35,886
ahead.

76
00:02:36,066 --> 00:02:38,144
It's called a dry brine.

77
00:02:38,324 --> 00:02:40,344
Take out the neck and the bag

78
00:02:40,344 --> 00:02:41,110
of giblets.

79
00:02:41,290 --> 00:02:42,846
Pat the turkey dry.

80
00:02:43,026 --> 00:02:45,385
Then rub it all over with salt,

81
00:02:45,385 --> 00:02:48,352
about one tablespoon of kosher salt for

82
00:02:48,352 --> 00:02:49,722
every four pounds,

83
00:02:49,722 --> 00:02:52,461
mixed with a little pepper and dried

84
00:02:52,461 --> 00:02:52,918
thyme.

85
00:02:53,098 --> 00:02:55,370
Get some under the skin of the

86
00:02:55,370 --> 00:02:56,279
breast, too.

87
00:02:56,628 --> 00:02:58,532
Then put it on a tray,

88
00:02:58,532 --> 00:03:01,562
uncovered, in the icebox for one or

89
00:03:01,562 --> 00:03:02,341
two days.

90
00:03:02,521 --> 00:03:05,029
The salt goes deep into the meat,

91
00:03:05,029 --> 00:03:07,461
and it holds the juices in while

92
00:03:07,461 --> 00:03:08,221
it roasts.

93
00:03:08,401 --> 00:03:10,921
And the skin dries out in the

94
00:03:10,921 --> 00:03:13,702
cold, so it roasts up crispy and

95
00:03:13,702 --> 00:03:14,311
golden.

96
00:03:14,491 --> 00:03:16,993
Mistake number two is skipping this,

97
00:03:16,993 --> 00:03:19,288
or putting the turkey in a bucket

98
00:03:19,288 --> 00:03:20,330
of salty water.

99
00:03:20,510 --> 00:03:22,022
That makes soggy skin,

100
00:03:22,022 --> 00:03:23,877
and a mess in your kitchen.

101
00:03:24,227 --> 00:03:25,558
And the timeline,

102
00:03:25,558 --> 00:03:28,140
honey, so Thursday isn't a panic.

103
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:31,384
Sunday, the turkey goes in the icebox

104
00:03:31,384 --> 00:03:32,047
to thaw.

105
00:03:32,227 --> 00:03:34,166
Tuesday, dry brine it.

106
00:03:34,346 --> 00:03:36,389
Wednesday, make the pies,

107
00:03:36,389 --> 00:03:39,413
the cranberry sauce and the stuffing,

108
00:03:39,413 --> 00:03:40,557
ready to bake.

109
00:03:40,737 --> 00:03:43,580
Thursday morning, the turkey comes out an

110
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:45,799
hour early and goes in the oven.

111
00:03:45,979 --> 00:03:47,980
Write it on a card and stick

112
00:03:47,980 --> 00:03:49,624
it on the refrigerator.

113
00:03:49,804 --> 00:03:52,761
That card has saved my Thanksgiving for

114
00:03:52,761 --> 00:03:53,671
forty years.

115
00:03:54,020 --> 00:03:55,744
On Thanksgiving morning,

116
00:03:55,744 --> 00:03:58,114
take the turkey out of the icebox

117
00:03:58,114 --> 00:04:00,197
an hour before it goes in the

118
00:04:00,197 --> 00:04:02,136
oven, so it's not ice cold.

119
00:04:02,316 --> 00:04:05,149
Heat the oven to four hundred twenty-five.

120
00:04:05,329 --> 00:04:06,664
Don't rinse it,

121
00:04:06,664 --> 00:04:07,198
honey.

122
00:04:07,378 --> 00:04:10,251
Rinsing a turkey splashes germs all over

123
00:04:10,251 --> 00:04:12,694
your sink and does nothing for the

124
00:04:12,694 --> 00:04:13,125
taste.

125
00:04:13,305 --> 00:04:16,105
Just pat it dry again with paper

126
00:04:16,105 --> 00:04:16,718
towels.

127
00:04:17,068 --> 00:04:19,748
Then stuff the inside of the bird,

128
00:04:19,748 --> 00:04:21,166
not with stuffing,

129
00:04:21,166 --> 00:04:23,294
but with a quartered onion,

130
00:04:23,294 --> 00:04:25,816
a lemon, a few cloves of garlic,

131
00:04:25,816 --> 00:04:27,471
and some fresh herbs.

132
00:04:27,651 --> 00:04:30,275
Sage, thyme and rosemary.

133
00:04:30,455 --> 00:04:33,334
They steam inside and perfume the meat.

134
00:04:33,514 --> 00:04:36,220
Rub the outside all over with soft

135
00:04:36,220 --> 00:04:36,777
butter.

136
00:04:36,957 --> 00:04:38,583
Tuck the wing tips under,

137
00:04:38,583 --> 00:04:40,861
like the turkey's taking a nap with

138
00:04:40,861 --> 00:04:42,553
its hands behind its head.

139
00:04:42,902 --> 00:04:44,584
If this is helping you,

140
00:04:44,584 --> 00:04:47,070
honey, tap the like button for me.

141
00:04:47,250 --> 00:04:49,944
It helps Grandma more than you know.

142
00:04:50,124 --> 00:04:52,678
And here's mistake number three.

143
00:04:52,858 --> 00:04:55,401
Cooking the stuffing inside the bird.

144
00:04:55,581 --> 00:04:57,623
By the time the stuffing in the

145
00:04:57,623 --> 00:04:59,731
middle is hot enough to be safe,

146
00:04:59,731 --> 00:05:01,641
the breast is dry as sawdust.

147
00:05:01,821 --> 00:05:04,044
Bake your stuffing in a dish on

148
00:05:04,044 --> 00:05:04,689
the side.

149
00:05:04,869 --> 00:05:06,633
It gets crispy on top,

150
00:05:06,633 --> 00:05:09,520
and the turkey cooks faster and more

151
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:10,082
evenly.

152
00:05:10,431 --> 00:05:12,373
Set the turkey on a rack in

153
00:05:12,373 --> 00:05:13,451
a roasting pan,

154
00:05:13,451 --> 00:05:14,170
breast up.

155
00:05:14,350 --> 00:05:15,814
Put a cup of broth,

156
00:05:15,814 --> 00:05:18,204
a chopped onion and a carrot in

157
00:05:18,204 --> 00:05:19,900
the bottom of the pan,

158
00:05:19,900 --> 00:05:20,979
for the gravy.

159
00:05:21,159 --> 00:05:23,850
Roast it at four twenty-five for thirty

160
00:05:23,850 --> 00:05:25,989
minutes to get the skin golden.

161
00:05:26,169 --> 00:05:28,604
Then turn the oven down to three

162
00:05:28,604 --> 00:05:30,964
twenty-five, and keep roasting.

163
00:05:31,144 --> 00:05:32,598
That's the answer,

164
00:05:32,598 --> 00:05:33,083
honey.

165
00:05:33,263 --> 00:05:34,797
Hot to start,

166
00:05:34,797 --> 00:05:36,096
then lower.

167
00:05:36,276 --> 00:05:38,853
My mother and the magazines were both

168
00:05:38,853 --> 00:05:39,619
half right.

169
00:05:39,969 --> 00:05:42,741
A fourteen pound turkey takes about three

170
00:05:42,741 --> 00:05:44,633
to three and a half hours in

171
00:05:44,633 --> 00:05:44,904
all.

172
00:05:45,084 --> 00:05:46,847
But don't trust the clock,

173
00:05:46,847 --> 00:05:49,425
and don't trust that little red popper

174
00:05:49,425 --> 00:05:51,527
that comes stuck in the turkey.

175
00:05:51,707 --> 00:05:54,400
It pops when the breast is already

176
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:55,271
overcooked.

177
00:05:55,451 --> 00:05:57,945
Mistake number four is going by time

178
00:05:57,945 --> 00:05:59,538
instead of temperature.

179
00:05:59,718 --> 00:06:01,471
Buy a meat thermometer.

180
00:06:01,651 --> 00:06:03,717
It costs about ten dollars,

181
00:06:03,717 --> 00:06:06,471
and it's the best ten dollars you'll

182
00:06:06,471 --> 00:06:07,619
spend all year.

183
00:06:07,968 --> 00:06:10,645
Put the thermometer in the thickest part

184
00:06:10,645 --> 00:06:11,582
of the breast,

185
00:06:11,582 --> 00:06:13,054
not touching the bone.

186
00:06:13,234 --> 00:06:15,675
Take the turkey out when the breast

187
00:06:15,675 --> 00:06:17,907
reads one hundred sixty degrees,

188
00:06:17,907 --> 00:06:20,278
and the thickest part of the thigh

189
00:06:20,278 --> 00:06:22,301
reads about one seventy-five.

190
00:06:22,481 --> 00:06:24,990
It keeps cooking while it rests,

191
00:06:24,990 --> 00:06:27,420
and the breast will climb up to

192
00:06:27,420 --> 00:06:29,145
a safe one sixty-five.

193
00:06:29,325 --> 00:06:31,820
If the skin gets too dark before

194
00:06:31,820 --> 00:06:34,393
that, lay a piece of foil loosely

195
00:06:34,393 --> 00:06:35,641
over the breast.

196
00:06:35,990 --> 00:06:38,773
And don't open the oven every fifteen

197
00:06:38,773 --> 00:06:40,051
minutes to baste,

198
00:06:40,051 --> 00:06:40,878
sweetheart.

199
00:06:41,058 --> 00:06:43,326
Every time you open the door,

200
00:06:43,326 --> 00:06:44,891
the oven loses heat,

201
00:06:44,891 --> 00:06:47,785
and the turkey takes longer and dries

202
00:06:47,785 --> 00:06:48,489
out more.

203
00:06:48,669 --> 00:06:50,891
With the dry brine and the butter,

204
00:06:50,891 --> 00:06:52,918
you don't need to baste at all.

205
00:06:53,098 --> 00:06:54,491
Peek through the window.

206
00:06:54,671 --> 00:06:56,056
Pearl used to say,

207
00:06:56,056 --> 00:06:58,363
a watched turkey never browns.

208
00:06:58,713 --> 00:07:01,039
So far, thaw it all the way,

209
00:07:01,039 --> 00:07:02,119
dry brine it,

210
00:07:02,119 --> 00:07:03,864
stuffing on the side,

211
00:07:03,864 --> 00:07:05,110
hot then lower,

212
00:07:05,110 --> 00:07:07,270
and go by the thermometer.

213
00:07:07,450 --> 00:07:09,064
Now the last mistake,

214
00:07:09,064 --> 00:07:11,447
the one I told you every family

215
00:07:11,447 --> 00:07:11,908
makes.

216
00:07:12,088 --> 00:07:14,234
Carving it the minute it comes out

217
00:07:14,234 --> 00:07:14,991
of the oven.

218
00:07:15,171 --> 00:07:17,054
When you cut a hot turkey,

219
00:07:17,054 --> 00:07:19,300
all the juices run out onto the

220
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:21,764
cutting board, and the meat on the

221
00:07:21,764 --> 00:07:22,706
plate is dry.

222
00:07:23,055 --> 00:07:25,438
Let it rest for at least thirty

223
00:07:25,438 --> 00:07:27,975
minutes, honey, and up to an hour

224
00:07:27,975 --> 00:07:29,127
for a big bird.

225
00:07:29,307 --> 00:07:31,658
Cover it loosely with foil and a

226
00:07:31,658 --> 00:07:32,907
clean dish towel.

227
00:07:33,087 --> 00:07:35,334
It stays hot for an hour,

228
00:07:35,334 --> 00:07:36,233
I promise.

229
00:07:36,413 --> 00:07:37,622
While it rests,

230
00:07:37,622 --> 00:07:40,604
the juices settle back into the meat.

231
00:07:40,784 --> 00:07:43,033
And this is the perfect time to

232
00:07:43,033 --> 00:07:44,122
make the gravy,

233
00:07:44,122 --> 00:07:45,210
warm the rolls,

234
00:07:45,210 --> 00:07:47,387
and put the side dishes in the

235
00:07:47,387 --> 00:07:47,750
oven.

236
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:49,043
For the gravy,

237
00:07:49,043 --> 00:07:51,468
pour the drippings from the pan into

238
00:07:51,468 --> 00:07:53,557
a big measuring cup and let the

239
00:07:53,557 --> 00:07:54,904
fat rise to the top.

240
00:07:55,084 --> 00:07:57,829
Spoon off four tablespoons of the fat

241
00:07:57,829 --> 00:07:59,017
into a saucepan,

242
00:07:59,017 --> 00:08:01,911
and whisk in four tablespoons of flour.

243
00:08:02,091 --> 00:08:03,437
Cook it two minutes.

244
00:08:03,617 --> 00:08:06,071
Then slowly whisk in four cups of

245
00:08:06,071 --> 00:08:07,855
the drippings and broth.

246
00:08:08,035 --> 00:08:10,187
Simmer it until it's thick,

247
00:08:10,187 --> 00:08:12,818
and taste it for salt and pepper.

248
00:08:13,168 --> 00:08:15,511
And scrape the roasting pan,

249
00:08:15,511 --> 00:08:16,431
sweetheart.

250
00:08:16,611 --> 00:08:17,963
Put it on the stove,

251
00:08:17,963 --> 00:08:19,519
pour in a little broth,

252
00:08:19,519 --> 00:08:21,683
and scrape up all the brown bits

253
00:08:21,683 --> 00:08:23,914
stuck to the bottom with a wooden

254
00:08:23,914 --> 00:08:24,320
spoon.

255
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:26,265
Pour that into the gravy.

256
00:08:26,445 --> 00:08:29,254
That's where the real flavor lives.

257
00:08:29,434 --> 00:08:31,948
My mother said a gravy without the

258
00:08:31,948 --> 00:08:34,461
pan scrapings is just brown paste.

259
00:08:34,811 --> 00:08:37,081
To carve, take off the whole legs

260
00:08:37,081 --> 00:08:39,351
first, cutting through the joint.

261
00:08:39,531 --> 00:08:42,028
Then cut the whole breast off the

262
00:08:42,028 --> 00:08:43,390
bone in one piece,

263
00:08:43,390 --> 00:08:44,373
on each side,

264
00:08:44,373 --> 00:08:46,643
and slice it across the grain,

265
00:08:46,643 --> 00:08:48,459
about a half inch thick.

266
00:08:48,639 --> 00:08:51,103
That way every slice has a little

267
00:08:51,103 --> 00:08:51,925
skin on it.

268
00:08:52,105 --> 00:08:54,644
It's much easier than slicing it on

269
00:08:54,644 --> 00:08:57,039
the bird, and nobody ends up with

270
00:08:57,039 --> 00:08:58,200
a shredded mess.

271
00:08:58,549 --> 00:09:00,204
And the leftovers,

272
00:09:00,204 --> 00:09:00,755
honey.

273
00:09:00,935 --> 00:09:03,268
Pull all the meat off the bones

274
00:09:03,268 --> 00:09:04,396
the same night,

275
00:09:04,396 --> 00:09:06,428
and put it in the icebox in

276
00:09:06,428 --> 00:09:09,438
containers, with a little gravy or broth

277
00:09:09,438 --> 00:09:10,792
so it stays moist.

278
00:09:10,972 --> 00:09:12,404
It keeps four days,

279
00:09:12,404 --> 00:09:14,513
or freezes for three months.

280
00:09:14,693 --> 00:09:17,336
And make soup from the bones on

281
00:09:17,336 --> 00:09:17,932
Friday.

282
00:09:18,112 --> 00:09:20,236
Pearl said the bones were the best

283
00:09:20,236 --> 00:09:21,423
part of the turkey,

284
00:09:21,423 --> 00:09:22,547
and she was right.

285
00:09:22,897 --> 00:09:24,372
So one more time.

286
00:09:24,552 --> 00:09:26,365
Thaw it in the icebox,

287
00:09:26,365 --> 00:09:28,673
a day for every five pounds.

288
00:09:28,853 --> 00:09:31,116
Dry brine it with salt a day

289
00:09:31,116 --> 00:09:32,167
or two ahead,

290
00:09:32,167 --> 00:09:32,975
uncovered.

291
00:09:33,155 --> 00:09:35,848
Herbs inside, butter outside,

292
00:09:35,848 --> 00:09:37,799
stuffing on the side.

293
00:09:37,979 --> 00:09:41,334
Four twenty-five, then three twenty-five.

294
00:09:41,514 --> 00:09:44,425
A thermometer, and out at one sixty

295
00:09:44,425 --> 00:09:45,589
in the breast.

296
00:09:45,769 --> 00:09:48,858
Rest it thirty minutes before you carve.

297
00:09:49,038 --> 00:09:52,501
That's how I've made fifty-nine juicy turkeys

298
00:09:52,501 --> 00:09:53,194
in a row.

299
00:09:53,543 --> 00:09:55,351
Tell me in the comments,

300
00:09:55,351 --> 00:09:56,179
sweetheart.

301
00:09:56,359 --> 00:09:58,971
Who cooks the turkey in your family?

302
00:09:59,151 --> 00:10:01,796
And has anybody ever had a turkey

303
00:10:01,796 --> 00:10:02,518
disaster?

304
00:10:02,698 --> 00:10:04,289
I'd love to hear it.

305
00:10:04,469 --> 00:10:07,555
The whole playlist of Grandma's recipes is

306
00:10:07,555 --> 00:10:09,539
right there on your screen,

307
00:10:09,539 --> 00:10:11,597
and I'll see you in the next

308
00:10:11,597 --> 00:10:12,038
video.

309
00:10:12,218 --> 00:10:13,716
Good night, honey.
